ayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Five second intake and submit storage budget\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022TriageService.SubmitReportAsync and session-log SaveChanges used by beginTurn persist use a 5 second connect and command budget. Timeouts map to backend_unavailable. No partial triage rows.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022TriageService.SubmitReportAsync and session-log SaveChanges used by beginTurn persist use a 5 second connect and command budget. Timeouts map to backend_unavailable. No partial triage rows.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TRIAGETODO-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Durable EXEC fallback and soft-delete id allocate\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022TodoExecutionService FindTodo falls back to ITodoService.GetByIdAsync with path normalization and rehydrates EXEC records. EfTodoService CreateAsync and GenerateNextTodoIdAsync use IgnoreQueryFilters for soft-deleted collisions. Batch create is transactional or compensating.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022TodoExecutionService FindTodo falls back to ITodoService.GetByIdAsync with path normalization and rehydrates EXEC records. EfTodoService CreateAsync and GenerateNextTodoIdAsync use IgnoreQueryFilters for soft-deleted collisions. Batch create is transactional or compensating.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TUN-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Tunnel Strategy Pattern\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022DI registration in \\u0060Program.cs\\u0060 reads \\u0060Mcp:Tunnel:Provider\\u0060, normalizes to uppercase, and uses \\u0060ActivatorUtilities.CreateInstance\\u003CT\\u003E\\u0060 to instantiate the matching provider (\\u0060NgrokTunnelProvider\\u0060, \\u0060CloudflareTunnelProvider\\u0060, or \\u0060FrpTunnelProvider\\u0060). The provider is registered as both a singleton and an \\u0060IHostedService\\u0060, conditionally on the provider name being non-empty.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TUN-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Tunnel Process Lifecycle\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060Process.Kill()\\u0060 is wrapped in a try-catch for \\u0060InvalidOperationException\\u0060 to handle races. \\u0060WaitForExit(5000)\\u0060 enforces a 5 s shutdown timeout. FRP config files written to temp storage are deleted on stop. All three providers log start, stop, and error events.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TUN-003\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Ngrok Auth Token Security\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022The ngrok auth token is passed via the \\u0060NGROK_AUTHTOKEN\\u0060 environment variable on the child process, rather than as a CLI argument, to prevent exposure in process listings and shell history.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TUN-004\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Tunnel provider inherits the interactive user environment\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Implements FR-MCP-141 and extends TR-MCP-TUN-003, which already establishes that NgrokTunnelProvider manipulates child-process environment variables. NgrokTunnelProvider SHALL take IProcessEnvironmentService and apply the interactive user\\u0027s USERPROFILE, HOME, APPDATA, and PATH to the ProcessStartInfo of the ngrok child process, so ngrok.yml resolves when the server runs under LocalSystem instead of the provider silently starting with the service account profile. The provider SHALL resolve the ngrok binary through ResolveExecutable against that enriched PATH rather than relying on the literal string ngrok. When the binary cannot be found the provider SHALL log at Warning rather than Error, and the message SHALL name the Windows-service and Store-alias causes and the available remedies. Recovered from origin/claude/busy-dubinsky. Note that develop ships Tunnel Provider empty and Ngrok.Enabled false, so this path is dormant under stock configuration.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXN-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Turn Transaction Coordinator\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Add \\u0060Mcp:TurnTransactions\\u0060, \\u0060ITurnTransactionCoordinator\\u0060, transaction request/result models, keyserver/subscriber client handoff, direct/HTTP/external broker pub-sub adapters, durable local pub-sub outbox/replay, degraded status, pending-commit cancellation, and first-party mutation gates. Mutation paths SHALL either use compensation-capable coordinator execution or fail closed before uncompensated side effects while required turn transactions are active.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete for PLAN-TURNTRANSACTIONS-001 first-slice scope.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060TurnTransactionCoordinator\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionPubSubServices\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionPubSubReplayWorker\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionFederationOperationApplyService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedMemoryService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedTodoMutationService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedRepoFileService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedPromptTemplateService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedRequirementsDocumentService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedSessionLogService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedToolRegistryService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedToolBucketService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedGraphRagService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedGitHubCliService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedIssueTodoSyncService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedVoiceConversationService\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedAgentPoolService\\u0060, \\u0060ClientMutationPolicy\\u0060, \\u0060FederationController\\u0060, \\u0060MemoryController\\u0060, \\u0060TodoController\\u0060, \\u0060McpServerMcpTools\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionalTodoWorkflow\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionCoordinatorTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionPubSubTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedMemoryServiceTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedTodoMutationServiceTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedSessionLogServiceTests\\u0060, \\u0060ClientMutationPolicyTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionalTodoWorkflowTests\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNAIUNIT-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022aiUnit Plan Review Gate\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Add a test-only aiUnit plan-review evidence gate for PLAN-TURNTRANSACTIONS-001. The gate SHALL validate committed aiUnit run-log evidence, require the reviewed scope to include FR-MCP-118 through FR-MCP-128 and TEST-MCP-158 through TEST-MCP-173, and fail when critical/high findings are present.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060PlanTransactionReviewTests\\u0060, \\u0060artifacts/aiunit-plan-review/aiunit-review-plan-20260612T060729.901Z.json\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNARCH-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Transaction Architecture Rounds\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Preserve a first architecture round that defines component ownership, trust boundaries, storage boundaries, threat model, rollback/audit rules, and gap analysis before implementation closeout.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060TurnTransactions-Architecture-Round1.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionPlanArtifactTests\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNAUDIT-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Transaction Audit Actions\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Transaction code SHALL record structured audit/session-log evidence for manifest sign/verify, commit/reject, abort, degraded, rollback, replay, retention, and aiUnit review events without deleting durable audit rows during rollback.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete for PLAN-TURNTRANSACTIONS-001 first-slice scope.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060TransactionSecurityStateStores\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionPubSubServices\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionCoordinator\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionGatedSessionLogService\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionsControllerTests\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionPubSubTests\\u0060, \\u0060DurableTransactionSecurityStorageTests\\u0060, \\u0060PlanTransactionReviewTests\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNBYRD-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Byrd v4 Transaction Gates\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Transaction implementation work SHALL be split into requirements-first, test-first, mock-first, implementation, refactor, and validation gates. Executed validation scopes SHALL exit with zero failures and zero skips; deferred work belongs in TODO/requirements state rather than skipped test placeholders.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete for PLAN-TURNTRANSACTIONS-001 first-slice scope.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060Functional-Requirements.md\\u0060, \\u0060Testing-Requirements.md\\u0060, \\u0060Requirements-Matrix.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionPlanArtifactTests\\u0060, \\u0060ValidateTraceability\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNCOMPAT-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Federation Compatibility\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Existing \\u0060Mcp:Federation\\u0060 HMAC envelopes SHALL remain backward compatible. Transaction crypto is additive and separate from federation envelope signing. Federation apply paths route through the coordinator, and federation control-plane mutations fail closed while required transaction gating is active until full compensation is designed.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete for PLAN-TURNTRANSACTIONS-001 first-slice scope.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060TurnTransactionFederationOperationApplyService\\u0060, \\u0060FederationController\\u0060, \\u0060FederationOperationApplyServiceTests\\u0060, \\u0060FederationControllerTests\\u0060, \\u0060FederationControllerPushTests\\u0060, \\u0060ClientMutationPolicyTests\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactions-Mutation-Endpoint-Audit.md\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNDESIGN-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Implementable Transaction Design Contracts\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Preserve a second design round that defines public DTOs, durable entities, options, interfaces, endpoint contracts, reason codes, audit payloads, XMLDoc obligations, canonicalization, test mappings, and explicit deferred scope before closeout.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060TurnTransactions-Design-Round2.md\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionSecurityModels\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionSecurityOptions\\u0060, \\u0060TransactionSecurityServices\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactions-Mutation-Endpoint-Audit.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionPlanArtifactTests\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-TXNDIAGRAMS-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Imported Diagram Traceability\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Imported Mermaid diagrams SHALL be preserved with stable IDs, source-section references, branch IDs, scope annotations, and test mappings. In-scope branches SHALL have tests; future quad-model, Curiosity, AoT, and weight-update branches SHALL remain explicitly deferred.\\n**Status:** \\u2705 Complete.\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060Quad-Model-Transactional-Diffgram-Plan.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactions-Architecture-Round1.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactions-Design-Round2.md\\u0060, \\u0060Testing-Requirements.md\\u0060, \\u0060TurnTransactionPlanArtifactTests\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use case EF storage multi-provider soft-delete\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Implement Use Case 4NF entities on McpDbContext with WorkspaceId max 1024, FK to Workspaces, soft-delete columns, Restrict/NoAction relationships, string FrId to RequirementEntity Kind=fr, global workspace query filters, and migrations for SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server named AddUseCaseSupport (timestamped). Audit emission for mutable entities per TR-MCP-DB-004.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use case CQRS commands and queries\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022All use case domain mutations and reads go through McpServer.Cqrs ICommand/IQuery handlers registered with Dispatcher. Controllers and MCP tools only dispatch; they do not open DbContext for domain logic.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-003\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use Case REST controller\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Thin /mcpserver/usecases dispatching CQRS. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-001; TEST-MCP-USECASE-002. Controller unit tests map Result failures to HTTP status codes.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-004\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use Case diagram service\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022DI-owned pure generator; mermaid \\u002B one extra format. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-005; TEST-MCP-USECASE-003.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-005\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use Case MCP tools, client, plugins\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022usecase_* tools; UseCaseClient live JSON parity; plugin-core \\u002B skills; REPL client.UseCases. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-001, FR-MCP-USECASE-007; TEST-MCP-USECASE-004, TEST-MCP-USECASE-010.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-006\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022FR projection, coverage, audit\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022linkedUseCases on FR get/list; coverage API; TR-MCP-DB-004 audit on mutable UC ops. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-003, FR-MCP-USECASE-006; TEST-MCP-USECASE-005, TEST-MCP-USECASE-007.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-007\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use Case UI hosting\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Static /usecases/ assets REST-only. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-007; TEST-MCP-USECASE-008.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-008\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Approval and product API\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022CQRS \\u002B REST for approval and ProductKey. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-008, FR-MCP-USECASE-009; TEST-MCP-USECASE-009.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-009\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Validation seams\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Docs matrix includes USECASE IDs; shared Realizes algorithm for DB findings. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-010; TEST-MCP-USECASE-005.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-010\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Use Case service deploy\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Nuke UpdateService only; config backup/restore; live health and routes. Covered by FR-MCP-USECASE-007; TEST-MCP-USECASE-011.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-011\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Graph storage\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022JSON column graph storage; multi-provider migrations; soft-delete and workspace filters. ACs AC-T11-1..3.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-012\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Diagram graph CQRS\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022GetGraph/PutGraph/Export handlers; thin controller. ACs AC-T12-1..2.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-013\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Diagram graph REST\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022GET/PUT diagram-graph; GET diagram kind=usecase format mermaid|plantuml; sequence remains. ACs AC-T13-1..3.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-014\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022UML serialization service\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Pure DI service graph to Mermaid and PlantUML. ACs AC-T14-1..2.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-015\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Canvas UI hosting\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Static /usecases/ canvas assets; palette; umlCanvas; REST-only. ACs AC-T15-1..2.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-USECASE-016\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Graph put audit\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Put graph emits DataAuditLog. AC-T16-1.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-VOICE-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Voice Conversation Service\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060VoiceConversationService\\u0060 manages the full voice session lifecycle: session creation with \\u0060CopilotInteractiveSession\\u0060 spawned via \\u0060DesktopProcessLauncher\\u0060 (or standard \\u0060Process.Start\\u0060), turn processing with tool-call loop (max \\u0060MaxToolSteps\\u0060 iterations), in-memory transcript storage, tool-call record tracking, and session cleanup. Configurable via \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions\\u0060 bound from \\u0060Mcp:Voice\\u0060 configuration section (model, timeouts, rate limits for writes/deletes per turn, transcript context limit).\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060VoiceConversationService\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions\\u0060, \\u0060CopilotInteractiveSession\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-VOICE-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Voice Controller REST API\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060VoiceController\\u0060 at \\u0060/mcpserver/voice/session/*\\u0060 exposes 8 endpoints: \\u0060POST /\\u0060 (create session with \\u0060DeviceId\\u0060/\\u0060Language\\u0060/\\u0060ClientName\\u0060), \\u0060GET /?deviceId=\\u0060 (find by device), \\u0060POST /{id}/turn\\u0060 (synchronous turn), \\u0060POST /{id}/turn/stream\\u0060 (SSE streaming turn), \\u0060POST /{id}/interrupt\\u0060 (cancel active turn), \\u0060POST /{id}/escape\\u0060 (send ESC chars to Copilot stdin), \\u0060GET /{id}\\u0060 (session status), \\u0060GET /{id}/transcript\\u0060 (transcript entries), \\u0060DELETE /{id}\\u0060 (destroy session). DTOs: \\u0060VoiceSessionCreateRequest/Response\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceTurnRequest/Response\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceInterruptResponse\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceSessionStatusDto\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceTranscriptEntryDto/Response\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceToolCallRecordDto\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceTurnStreamEvent\\u0060.\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060VoiceController\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceConversationContracts\\u0060\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-VOICE-003\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Voice Session Lifecycle Management\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022One active session per device enforced via \\u0060DeviceId\\u0060 lookup; creating a new session for a device with an active session returns the existing session. Idle timeout (\\u0060SessionIdleTimeoutMinutes\\u0060, default 15) triggers the configured idle-shutdown prompt sent to Copilot, waits for the configured sentinel response, then terminates the session. \\u0060UseDesktopLaunch\\u0060 option (default true) selects \\u0060CreateProcessAsUser\\u0060 for Windows service context.\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060VoiceConversationService.OnIdleCleanupTick\\u0060 / \\u0060CleanupIdleSessionsAsync\\u0060 (60s timer-driven idle-shutdown orchestrator), \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions.SessionIdleTimeoutMinutes\\u0060, \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions.IdleShutdownCommand\\u0060 (config string sent to Copilot), \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions.IdleShutdownSentinel\\u0060 (config string awaited as the shutdown confirmation). Note: \\u0060IdleShutdownCommand\\u0060 and \\u0060IdleShutdownSentinel\\u0060 are configured strings on \\u0060VoiceConversationOptions\\u0060, not CLR message types.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-VOICE-004\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Interactive Presence Signals on Stream State Changes\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022On interactive stream disconnect, the runtime SHALL send \\u0060User is AFK.\\u0060 to the associated interactive agent session.\\nOn interactive stream reconnect, after response stream establishment, the runtime SHALL send \\u0060User is here.\\u0060 to the associated interactive agent session.\\n\\nPresence signaling SHALL be excluded from one-shot sessions.\\n\\n**Status:** \\uD83D\\uDD34 Planned\\n\\n**Covered by:** \\u0060VoiceConversationService\\u0060 *(planned extension)*, \\u0060AgentPoolStreamService\\u0060 *(planned)*\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Web UI Ownership Boundary\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Web UI implementation work for the former McpServer.UI.Core and McpServer.Director surfaces SHALL be owned by the McpServerManager repository. This repository SHALL keep only server-side contracts, API behavior, and compatibility documentation required by those external UI clients.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022deferred\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Deferred to McpServerManager; this repository owns only server-side contracts and compatibility documentation.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022New Web UI implementation code is not added under this repository moved UI surfaces.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred to McpServerManager.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Server-side API changes needed by McpServerManager are tracked as MCP FR/TR/TEST items in this repository.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Cross-repo handoffs identify the owning repository and do not silently reopen moved UI projects here.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Web UI API Compatibility Contract\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Server APIs consumed by external web-management clients SHALL remain documented and version-compatible across McpServer and McpServerManager. Breaking API changes require explicit requirements updates, migration notes, and tests in the server repository before deployment.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022deferred\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022API changes intended for web-management clients name the consuming route, DTO, and owning client surface.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Breaking changes include a migration note and compatibility test coverage.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Generated requirements/wiki output reflects the current cross-repo API contract.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-003\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Web UI Authentication And Workspace Boundary\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022External web-management clients SHALL authenticate through the existing MCP workspace auth/token model and SHALL preserve workspace isolation. This repository SHALL provide the server-side policy and tests; client UX and screen implementation remain in McpServerManager.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022deferred\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Web-client API calls use existing workspace-token/OIDC policy behavior rather than a new parallel auth path.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Workspace-scoped requests remain isolated by the resolved workspace path.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Any new server endpoint used by web clients includes auth and workspace-isolation tests.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-004\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Web UI Deployment And Handoff Documentation\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Deployment guidance for web-management surfaces SHALL distinguish server deployment in this repository from UI/client deployment in McpServerManager. This repository SHALL document only the server prerequisites, endpoint contracts, and compatibility expectations needed for the external UI.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022deferred\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Server deployment docs do not instruct agents to deploy moved UI projects from this repository.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Handoff docs name McpServerManager as the owner for UI implementation and client deployment.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Server readiness/config validation covers the endpoints and auth policy that external UI clients depend on.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022Deferred until next integration slice.\u0022}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022docs/wiki.yaml export configuration loader and renderer integration\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Implement a typed YamlDotNet-backed docs/wiki.yaml loader, validation layer, and wiki renderer integration shared by database-backed and document-backed requirements services.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022completed\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Do not parse YAML with string or regex logic. Resolve docs/wiki.yaml under the active workspace through RequirementsOptions.WikiConfigPath.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022RequirementsOptions exposes WikiConfigPath defaulting to docs/wiki.yaml, and services resolve it under the active workspace path or configured requirements root.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022RequirementsWikiExportConfig models deserialize docs/wiki.yaml with YamlDotNet into typed objects, with no line-based or regex YAML parsing.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Validation rejects unsupported schema values, missing required fields, duplicate document ids, duplicate targets per platform, path traversal, reserved managed target files, unsupported generated sources, invalid platform names, missing source files, and navigation/document mismatches.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC4\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Both RequirementsDatabaseDocumentService.GenerateWikiAsync and RequirementsDocumentService.GenerateWikiAsync share the same config loader and renderer path.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC5\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022The exporter validates all configured content before calling RequirementsDocumentExportWriter so invalid config leaves existing export files unchanged.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC6\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Generated platform side files remain managed by the exporter, including .mcp-requirements-manifest.json, GitHub _Sidebar.md and _Footer.md, and Azure .order files.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Marker writer default wiki.yaml serializer\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Extend MarkerFileService.WriteMarkerAsync with an idempotent default wiki.yaml writer that builds typed objects and serializes them with YamlDotNet before writing docs/wiki.yaml.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022completed\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022The writer must run as part of marker creation and must preserve user-authored docs/wiki.yaml files.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022MarkerFileService computes the default wiki config path as workspace-root/docs/wiki.yaml and creates the docs directory when needed.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022MarkerFileService checks for an existing docs/wiki.yaml before writing and skips creation when the file already exists.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Default wiki config is represented by typed or dictionary objects and serialized with the existing YamlDotNet serializer.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC4\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022The default config targets Home.md, Functional-Requirements.md, Technical-Requirements.md, Testing-Requirements.md, TR-per-FR-Mapping.md, and Requirements-Matrix.md on both platforms.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC5\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022A failure to create the default wiki.yaml is logged through the marker writer warning path and does not leave a partially written file.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Service\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022CRUD operations for workspace entities persisted in EF Core SQLite. Auto-port assignment starts at base 7147 and increments from the current maximum registered port. Init scaffolding creates the workspace directory, \\u0060docs/Project/TODO.yaml\\u0060, \\u0060docs/sessions/\\u0060, \\u0060docs/external/\\u0060, and \\u0060mcp.db\\u0060.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-003\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Process Manager\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Manages workspace marker file lifecycle. On startup, generates tokens and writes \\u0060AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml\\u0060 marker files for all registered workspaces - all pointing to the single shared host port. On stop, removes marker files. No longer spawns child \\u0060WebApplication\\u0060 instances (replaced by single-app multi-tenant model, see TR-MCP-MT-001 through TR-MCP-MT-003).\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-004\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Controller\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022REST API at \\u0060/mcpserver/workspace\\u0060 with Base64URL-encoded path keys. Provides create, read, update, delete, init, start, stop, status, and prompt (GET/PUT) endpoints. All \\u0060/mcpserver/*\\u0060 routes protected by \\u0060WorkspaceAuthMiddleware\\u0060 (per-workspace token).\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-005\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Marker File Service\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060MarkerFileService.WriteMarkerAsync\\u0060 writes \\u0060AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml\\u0060 to the workspace root. All markers point to the same shared host port. Uses Handlebars.Net templating with full workspace context. The marker template MUST be loaded from \\u0060templates/prompt-templates.yaml\\u0060 via \\u0060PromptTemplateService\\u0060 (id: \\u0060default-marker-prompt\\u0060). **CRITICAL**: If the template cannot be loaded (missing file, invalid YAML, or missing ID), the service must log a critical error and shut down the server immediately. Fallback to hardcoded templates is PROHIBITED. The YAML file contains port, \\u0060baseUrl\\u0060, all endpoint paths, process PID, \\u0060startedAt\\u0060 timestamp, workspace name, per-workspace auth token (\\u0060apiKey\\u0060), and a machine-readable \\u0060prompt\\u0060 block. Agents should send \\u0060X-Workspace-Path\\u0060 header for workspace targeting.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-006\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Host Controller Isolation\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022*Obsolete.* Replaced by single-app multi-tenant model (TR-MCP-MT-002). \\u0060ExcludeControllerFeatureProvider\\u0060 can be removed.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-007\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Auto-Start on Service Startup\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060WorkspaceProcessManager\\u0060, as an \\u0060IHostedService\\u0060, queries all registered workspaces on \\u0060StartAsync\\u0060 and writes marker files for each. Failures on individual workspace marker writes are logged and skipped rather than aborting global startup.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-008\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Workspace Auto-Init and Auto-Start on Creation\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060WorkspaceController\\u0060 POST calls \\u0060WorkspaceService.InitAsync\\u0060 to scaffold the directory structure, then calls \\u0060WorkspaceProcessManager.StartAsync\\u0060 to bring the host online, all within a single request, before returning 201 Created.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-009\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Primary Workspace Detection and IsEnabled Gating\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060WorkspaceProcessManager.IHostedService.StartAsync\\u0060 resolves the primary workspace: first by \\u0060IsPrimary = true\\u0060 \\u002B lowest port among enabled workspaces; then by lowest-port enabled workspace if none is marked primary. For the primary workspace, only a marker file is written - no child \\u0060WebApplication\\u0060 is created. Workspaces with \\u0060IsEnabled = false\\u0060 are skipped during auto-start but can be started manually.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-MCP-WS-UI-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022McpServer Management Web UI\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Reserved/planned: web-based management UI for workspace and server administration. Tracks FR-MCP-031.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-PLANNED-013A\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022\\u0060AddControllers().ConfigureApiBehaviorOptions\\u0060 installs an \\u0060InvalidModelStateResponseFactory\\u0060 that produces \\u0060application/problem\\u002Bjson\\u0060 responses for body-binding failures on \\u0060/mcpserver/*\\u0060 endpoints. The factory strips the action parameter name (\\u0060dto\\u0060, \\u0060body\\u0060, \\u0060turn\\u0060) from the \\u0060errors\\u0060 keys, replacing them with \\u0060$\\u0060 so callers see the canonical JSON root marker instead of a misleading wrapper field name. \\u0060SessionLogController.SubmitAsync\\u0060 and \\u0060GetByIdAsync\\u0060 use \\u0060ValidationProblem\\u0060 for domain validation to keep the response shape uniform.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-PLANNED-CORE-014\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Problem\\u002BJSON response factory for model binding failures\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022AddControllers().ConfigureApiBehaviorOptions installs an InvalidModelStateResponseFactory that produces application/problem\\u002Bjson responses for body-binding failures on /mcpserver/* endpoints. The factory strips the action parameter name (dto, body, turn) from the errors keys, replacing them with $ so callers see the canonical JSON root marker instead of a misleading wrapper field name. SessionLogController.SubmitAsync and GetByIdAsync use ValidationProblem for domain validation to keep the response shape uniform.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022InvalidModelStateResponseFactory produces application/problem\\u002Bjson for body-binding failures on /mcpserver/* endpoints\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Factory strips action parameter names (dto, body, turn) and replaces with $ marker\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022SessionLogController.SubmitAsync and GetByIdAsync use ValidationProblem for domain validation\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-4\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Response shape is uniform across model binding and domain validation failures\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-SUPPORT-010E\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Stateless lifecycle controller \\u002B client \\u002B tool adapters\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022SessionLogController exposes open/begin/complete/fail keyed by ids; SessionLogClient and MCP tools delegate; UpsertTurnAsync underpins all.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-SUPPORT-010F\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Merge-on-null mapping for partial submits\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022MapDtoToEntity merges non-null scalars; UpsertTurns passes mergeOmittedFields:true; collections append-only.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-SUPPORT-CORE-014\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Stateless lifecycle controller with client and tool adapters\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022SessionLogController exposes open/begin/complete/fail endpoints keyed by ids; SessionLogClient and MCP tools delegate to these endpoints; UpsertTurnAsync underpins all lifecycle operations to provide a single point of truth for turn state transitions.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022SessionLogController exposes open/begin/complete/fail lifecycle endpoints keyed by ids\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022SessionLogClient delegates to SessionLogController lifecycle endpoints\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022MCP tools delegate to SessionLogController lifecycle endpoints\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-4\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022UpsertTurnAsync is the single point of truth for all turn state transitions\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-SUPPORT-CORE-015\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Merge-on-null mapping for partial submits\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022MapDtoToEntity merges non-null scalars when mapping DTOs to entities; UpsertTurns passes mergeOmittedFields:true to enable partial updates; collections use append-only semantics to preserve existing items when partial submits occur.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022MapDtoToEntity merges only non-null scalars from DTO to entity\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022UpsertTurns passes mergeOmittedFields:true to enable partial updates\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Collections use append-only semantics during partial submits\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-4\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Existing entity fields not present in DTO remain unchanged\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-SUPPORT-LOG-010\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Session-log ProblemDetails contract\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Session-log REST endpoints SHALL return application/problem\\u002Bjson for malformed JSON binding and domain validation failures. Error keys SHALL identify the JSON root or offending domain field rather than leaking action parameter names such as dto.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022completed\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022PLAN-TRACEABILITY-AUDIT-001 DB-backed sync before wiki regeneration.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-TEST-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022TR-TEST-001\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link TR-TEST-001.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022medium\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-TRIAGE-CLIENT-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Typed triage dashboard client endpoints\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022SharpNinja.McpServer.Client exposes typed triage dashboard and run-history methods backed by REST endpoints for queue contents, groupings, AI triage runs, results, and current status.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022pending\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:null,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022McpServerClient.Triage exposes methods to query the dashboard, query runs, and get an individual run.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022REST and client request/response models preserve status, result JSON, raw output, prompt metadata, created TODO id, errors, timestamps, and workspace filters.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022Existing QueryGroupsAsync, GetGroupAsync, and GetReportAsync remain compatible for the planned shared UI.Core view model.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:false,\u0022evidence\u0022:null}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022TR-TRIAGE-CLIENT-002\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Typed triage TODO client endpoint\u0022,\u0022Body\u0022:\u0022REST, service, and SharpNinja.McpServer.Client typed triage APIs expose a triage-created TODO index with TODO IDs, created-at datetimes, workspace filters, group IDs, run IDs, and current triage status context.\u0022,\u0022WorkspaceId\u0022:\u0022F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Status\u0022:\u0022completed\u0022,\u0022Notes\u0022:\u0022Typed service, REST controller, and client endpoint now expose triage-created TODO IDs and persisted creation timestamps.\u0022,\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\u0022:[{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-1\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022McpServerClient.Triage exposes a typed method for querying triage-created TODOs.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022TriageClientTests.QueryCreatedTodosAsync_SendsWorkspaceFilter\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-2\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022The REST endpoint returns a stable JSON contract with total count and item collection fields.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022TriageControllerTests.QueryCreatedTodosAsync_ReturnsCreatedTodoIndex\u0022},{\u0022id\u0022:\u0022ac-3\u0022,\u0022text\u0022:\u0022The implementation uses persisted TODO creation timestamps instead of inferring creation time from triage run completion.\u0022,\u0022isSatisfied\u0022:true,\u0022evidence\u0022:\u0022TriageServiceTests.QueryCreatedTodosAsync_ReturnsTodoIdsCreatedAtUtcAndTriageContext\u0022}],\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\u0022:\u0022layer-1\u0022,\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\u0022:null}]}"}]},"id":21,"jsonrpc":"2.0"}
