nicalDetails\u0022:[\u0022Root symptom: app dashboard/API/plugin surfaces can show workspace TODO/session-log counts that do not match the SQL-backed data after migration; evidence showed F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\aiUnit active with 2 TODOs and 0 session logs while SQL data existed, and F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer data also exists.\u0022,\u0022Data-loss guard: begin remediation by proving data is present in the configured SQL Server/LocalDB store before changing code. Record row counts by workspace for TodoItems and SessionLogs and verify the configured connection string points at the intended existing database.\u0022,\u0022Expected behavior: app dashboard counts, REST list/detail endpoints, plugin TODO/session-log queries, and MCP client calls must all resolve the same active workspace and return the same workspace-scoped data.\u0022,\u0022Likely root cause: workspace-scoped EF query filters capture DbContext workspace state before WorkspaceResolutionMiddleware populates WorkspaceContext for some app/API/session-log read paths; TODO paths appear to have explicit workspace override while SessionLogService likely does not.\u0022,\u0022Remediation path: add a request-scoped DbContext or explicit workspace override for SessionLogService read/write/query paths equivalent to the TODO service pattern, and ensure controller/app/plugin paths never query with an empty or stale workspace id unless intentionally performing cross-workspace admin reads.\u0022,\u0022Regression coverage must include at least two workspaces with distinct TODO/session-log rows, one active workspace switch, app/API query paths, plugin query paths, and a stale-DbContext construction scenario.\u0022,\u0022Validation must prove no migration/data loss, correct visibility for F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer and F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\aiUnit, zero failures and zero skips in the focused scope, and deployment only through Nuke if a service update is required.\u0022],\u0022ImplementationTasks\u0022:[{\