L/plugin/client/dashboard parity matched F:\\\\GitHub\\\\McpServer todos=63/sessionLogs=320 and F:\\\\GitHub\\\\aiUnit todos=2/sessionLogs=3 after Nuke/gsudo redeploy. Diagnosed the remaining full-integration blocker as PairingWebApplicationFactory using the repository content root with the real appsettings source and no isolated DB/no-op projection writer; isolated it to temp workspace/data storage and suppressed workspace projection writes. Final validation passed with zero skips: full McpServer.Support.Mcp.IntegrationTests 194/194, McpServer.Support.Mcp.Tests 889/889, McpServer.Client.Tests 184/184, McpServer.Repl.Core.Tests 612/612, focused McpServerManager web workspace tests 3/3.\u0022,\u0022Remaining\u0022:\u0022Closed after fixing the unrelated integration guarded-file mutation and rerunning the full integration project with zero failures and zero skips.\u0022,\u0022PriorityNote\u0022:null,\u0022Reference\u0022:null,\u0022Phase\u0022:null,\u0022DependsOn\u0022:null,\u0022FunctionalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022FR-MCP-043\u0022,\u0022FR-SUPPORT-010A\u0022,\u0022FR-SUPPORT-010C\u0022],\u0022TechnicalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022TR-MCP-MT-001\u0022,\u0022TR-MCP-MT-003A\u0022,\u0022TR-MCP-TODO-005\u0022],\u0022IdempotencyKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022BUG-HOOKEVENTNAME-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Add hookEventName to session/compact plugin hook outputs\u0022,\u0022Section\u0022:\u0022Backlog\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true,\u0022Estimate\u0022:null,\u0022Note\u0022:null,\u0022Description\u0022:[\u0022Several MCP plugin hook scripts emit hookSpecificOutput WITHOUT the required hookEventName field, which Claude Code rejects (non-blocking) as a schema violation. Same class as the fixed Bug A (plan-modified.sh / plan-approved.sh) but for non-PostToolUse events.\\nAffected scripts across plugins (claude-code, claude-cowork, grok, copilot, codex, cline, cline-v2, and the non-git marketplace mirror):\\n- session-start.sh: degraded / MCP_UNTRUSTED / final status emits lack hookEventName (SessionStart) and use non-spec fields (sessionId, mcpBaseUrl).\\n- session-end.sh: emits hookSpecificOutput; SessionEnd likely does not support it. Emit {} instead.\\n- pre-compact.sh: PreCompact emits lack hookEventName.\\n- post-compact.sh: PostCompact emits lack hookEventName; per CC docs PostCompact cannot inject context (use SessionStart matcher:compact for additionalContext).\\nAuthoritative schema: hookEventName is required inside hookSpecificOutput for every event that supports it; status-only reports should emit {} or exit 0. Ref https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md\\n\u0022],\u0022TechnicalDetails\u0022:[\u0022Byrd TDD: add failing bats coverage first (mirror the Bug A tests in claude-code-plugin tests/hooks.bats), then patch. Rule: status-only hookSpecificOutput emits become {}; context-injecting emits use {hookSpecificOutput:{hookEventName:\\u003CEvent\\u003E, additionalContext:...}} only. Validate each plugin bats suite green (zero fail/skip), then commit scoped and push to github main, same workflow as hook bugs A/B (commits cc96085 etc, 2026-05-30). Related: bugs A (missing hookEventName PostToolUse) and B (Stop invalid status) already fixed and pushed across 9 plugins on 2026-05-30.\\n\u0022],\u0022ImplementationTasks\u0022:null,\u0022CompletedDate\u0022:null,\u0022DoneSummary\u0022:\u0022SessionStart, SessionEnd, PreCompact, and PostCompact hook scripts now emit schema-valid no-op JSON for status-only outcomes; PostCompact no longer emits unsupported additionalContext. Added/updated hook Bats coverage and pushed affected plugin repos to origin/main.\u0022,\u0022Remaining\u0022:null,\u0022PriorityNote\u0022:null,\u0022Reference\u0022:null,\u0022Phase\u0022:null,\u0022DependsOn\u0022:null,\u0022FunctionalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022FR-MCP-115\u0022],\u0022TechnicalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022TR-MCP-PLUGIN-009\u0022],\u0022IdempotencyKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022BUG-REQUPDATE-001\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Fix Codex plugin requirements update priority path\u0022,\u0022Section\u0022:\u0022Backlog\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true,\u0022Estimate\u0022:null,\u0022Note\u0022:\u00222026-06-01: Closed. openSession schema fix (plugin 89b219f), repl-invoke-shim.bats 47/0/0, live priority=high verified on all 6 targets.\u0022,\u0022Description\u0022:[\u0022Fix the Codex plugin workflow.requirements.updateFr, updateTr, and updateTest path so existing requirement records can be updated, including priority changes to high.\u0022,\u0022The bug was observed when trying to move newly created planning requirements from medium to high priority through the Codex MCP plugin.\u0022,\u0022Canonical behavior is that updateFr, updateTr, and updateTest pass the supplied YAML fields through the wrapper and return a successful update result instead of failing inside Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1.\u0022,\u0022Requirement coverage is FR-MCP-106, TR-MCP-PLUGIN-008, and TEST-MCP-142.\u0022],\u0022TechnicalDetails\u0022:[\u0022Start with a failing Bats test in F:/GitHub/mcpserver-codex-plugin/tests/repl-invoke-shim.bats that reproduces priority updates for FR, TR, and TEST records.\u0022,\u0022Inspect F:/GitHub/mcpserver-codex-plugin/lib/repl-invoke.sh requirements fallback handling and the typed method mapping for updateFr, updateTr, and updateTest.\u0022,\u0022Fix the smallest wrapper or shim defect so update payloads preserve id, priority, title, description, status, and notes fields.\u0022,\u0022Validate with focused Bats tests through C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe and then prove live update on FR-MCP-106, TR-MCP-PLUGIN-008, and TEST-MCP-142.\u0022],\u0022ImplementationTasks\u0022:[{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 1 add failing Bats coverage for requirements update priority mutation across FR TR and TEST\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 2 patch the Codex plugin requirements update fallback or typed mapping\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 3 prior focused Bats validation with zero failures and zero skips\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 4 add or refresh failing coverage for the current live-shaped priority update failure and create-priority default mismatch\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 5 rerun focused Bats validation through C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe with zero failures and zero skips\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 6 verify live workflow.requirements.updateFr updateTr and updateTest can set high priority records on FR-MCP-108 TR-MCP-TODO-009 TEST-MCP-144 and original targets\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true},{\u0022Task\u0022:\u0022Gate 7 update MCP TODO/session log evidence and close BUG-REQUPDATE-001\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true}],\u0022CompletedDate\u0022:null,\u0022DoneSummary\u0022:\u0022Closed via clean BUG-REQUPDATE slice.\\n\\nRoot cause (final): workflow.sessionlog.openSession schema validator in\\nmcpserver-codex-plugin/lib/repl-invoke.sh required a sessionId param, rejecting\\nthe handler\\u0027s auto-generate path (and begin_turn empty-param auto-open) with\\nschema_validation_failed. This blocked clean focused-suite validation.\\n\\nFix: dropped the sessionId requirement (title still required); fully backward\\ncompatible (session-start.sh still supplies sessionId).\\n\\nValidation (zero failures, zero skips):\\n- Focused Bats: tests/repl-invoke-shim.bats = 47 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip (exit 0),\\n  run serially to avoid shared-cache cross-run contamination.\\n- Requirements update shim coverage (tests 27-34) green: updateFr/updateTr/\\n  updateTest typed-fallback preserve\\u002Bhydrate priority/status/notes; createFr\\n  cannot swallow high priority.\\n- Live server verification: GET-\\u003EPUT(priority:high)-\\u003EGET round-trip PASS for\\n  FR-MCP-106, TR-MCP-PLUGIN-008, TEST-MCP-142 and FR-MCP-108, TR-MCP-TODO-009,\\n  TEST-MCP-144. priority:high preserved, no