],\u0022TechnicalDetails\u0022:[\u0022Acceptance criteria:\u0022,\u0022- Codex and ClaudeCode SessionStart create canonical session ids with a suffix and only mark a local session active after workflow.sessionlog.openSession succeeds server-side.\u0022,\u0022- UserPromptSubmit, Stop, code-verify, CompleteTurn, appendActions, and Status all read and write the same workspace/session-scoped cache and do not reuse stale flat cache after marker regeneration or server restart.\u0022,\u0022- Codex Status reports agent Codex, uses the active workspace scoped cache, and does not require removed Bash status scripts.\u0022,\u0022- appendActions persists edit, design_decision, and commit actions including sha, branch, message, and filePath without emitting empty action objects.\u0022,\u0022- When UpsertTurn or Submit fails, the plugin returns an observable failure and durable replay record instead of reporting success while only writing a failsafe file.\u0022,\u0022- End-to-end validation after fresh marker regeneration and after server restart shows beginTurn, wiki commit appendActions, completeTurn, and server GET for the active session all persisted with the expected turn and actions.\u0022,\u0022Implementation notes:\u0022,\u0022- Port or share cache-scope behavior for the PowerShell runtime; plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1 currently accepts CacheMode but does not implement scoped workspace/session cache selection.\u0022,\u0022- Replace handcrafted session id construction in PowerShell hooks with the same slugged canonical generator used by the shell path or server helpers.\u0022,\u0022- Fix wrapper environment defaults so PLUGIN_ROOT_OVERRIDE is not used as the normal Status cache root and MCP_PLUGIN_HOST is set before mcp-status.ps1 loads plugin-env.ps1.\u0022,\u0022- Replace regex/line-based action parsing in repl-invoke.ps1 with structured YAML or object conversion and propagate persistence errors to the caller and stop gate.\u0022,\u0022- Sync generated Codex and Claude plugin packages from the corrected core runtime and update stale manifest/tests that still expect removed Bash status scripts.\u0022],\u0022ImplementationTasks\u0022:null,\u0022CompletedDate\u0022:null,\u0022DoneSummary\u0022:\u0022Fixed plugin PowerShell session/runtime drift. Session IDs now include canonical suffixes, current-turn and session-state YAML writes use object serialization, REPL persistence parses actions through structured YAML, stale two-part session IDs are normalized, missing server sessions fall back to SubmitAsync, and Upsert/Submit failures are observable instead of being piped away. Synced all agent plugin packages and installed caches to 1.18.0. Validation passed: Invoke-Pester plugins/core/test-fixtures/pester returned 356 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; .\\\\build.ps1 SyncAgentPlugins succeeded; .\\\\build.ps1 ValidatePluginPowerShellOnly succeeded across 9 package roots; git diff --check was clean across McpServer and touched plugin repos.\u0022,\u0022Remaining\u0022:\u0022Completed. Plugin PowerShell session IDs, current-turn cache serialization, action parsing, persistence failure surfacing, stale session recovery, requirements skill guidance, staged/generated packages, clean manifests, and installed caches were updated and validated.\u0022,\u0022PriorityNote\u0022:null,\u0022Reference\u0022:null,\u0022Phase\u0022:null,\u0022DependsOn\u0022:null,\u0022FunctionalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022FR-MCP-TRIAGE-002\u0022],\u0022TechnicalRequirements\u0022:[\u0022TR-MCP-TRIAGE-004\u0022],\u0022IdempotencyKey\u0022:null},{\u0022Id\u0022:\u0022BUG-TRIAGE-010\u0022,\u0022Title\u0022:\u0022Persist structured acceptance criteria for all requirement types\u0022,\u0022Section\u0022:\u0022Backlog\u0022,\u0022Priority\u0022:\u0022high\u0022,\u0022Done\u0022:true,\u0022Estimate\u0022:null,\u0022Note\u0022:null,\u0022Description\u0022:[\u0022Requirement create/update paths return success while silently dropping structured acceptanceCriteria. Reports confirm