"id":"ac-1","text":"code-verify catches disk-full and enforces wrapper timeout","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":null}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-VOICE-001","Title":"Voice Conversation Service","Body":"\u0060VoiceConversationService\u0060 manages the full voice session lifecycle: session creation with \u0060CopilotInteractiveSession\u0060 spawned via \u0060DesktopProcessLauncher\u0060 (or standard \u0060Process.Start\u0060), turn processing with tool-call loop (max \u0060MaxToolSteps\u0060 iterations), in-memory transcript storage, tool-call record tracking, and session cleanup. Configurable via \u0060VoiceConversationOptions\u0060 bound from \u0060Mcp:Voice\u0060 configuration section (model, timeouts, rate limits for writes/deletes per turn, transcript context limit).\n**Covered by:** \u0060VoiceConversationService\u0060, \u0060VoiceConversationOptions\u0060, \u0060CopilotInteractiveSession\u0060","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-VOICE-002","Title":"Voice Controller REST API","Body":"\u0060VoiceController\u0060 at \u0060/mcpserver/voice/session/*\u0060 exposes 8 endpoints: \u0060POST /\u0060 (create session with \u0060DeviceId\u0060/\u0060Language\u0060/\u0060ClientName\u0060), \u0060GET /?deviceId=\u0060 (find by device), \u0060POST /{id}/turn\u0060 (synchronous turn), \u0060POST /{id}/turn/stream\u0060 (SSE streaming turn), \u0060POST /{id}/interrupt\u0060 (cancel active turn), \u0060POST /{id}/escape\u0060 (send ESC chars to Copilot stdin), \u0060GET /{id}\u0060 (session status), \u0060GET /{id}/transcript\u0060 (transcript entries), \u0060DELETE /{id}\u0060 (destroy session). DTOs: \u0060VoiceSessionCreateRequest/Response\u0060, \u0060VoiceTurnRequest/Response\u0060, \u0060VoiceInterruptResponse\u0060, \u0060VoiceSessionStatusDto\u0060, \u0060VoiceTranscriptEntryDto/Response\u0060, \u0060VoiceToolCallRecordDto\u0060, \u0060VoiceTurnStreamEvent\u0060.\n**Covered by:** \u0060VoiceController\u0060, \u0060VoiceConversationContracts\u0060","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-VOICE-003","Title":"Voice Session Lifecycle Management","Body":"One active session per device enforced via \u0060DeviceId\u0060 lookup; creating a new session for a device with an active session returns the existing session. Idle timeout (\u0060SessionIdleTimeoutMinutes\u0060, default 15) triggers the configured idle-shutdown prompt sent to Copilot, waits for the configured sentinel response, then terminates the session. \u0060UseDesktopLaunch\u0060 option (default true) selects \u0060CreateProcessAsUser\u0060 for Windows service context.\n**Covered by:** \u0060VoiceConversationService.OnIdleCleanupTick\u0060 / \u0060CleanupIdleSessionsAsync\u0060 (60s timer-driven idle-shutdown orchestrator), \u0060VoiceConversationOptions.SessionIdleTimeoutMinutes\u0060, \u0060VoiceConversationOptions.IdleShutdownCommand\u0060 (config string sent to Copilot), \u0060VoiceConversationOptions.IdleShutdownSentinel\u0060 (config string awaited as the shutdown confirmation). Note: \u0060IdleShutdownCommand\u0060 and \u0060IdleShutdownSentinel\u0060 are configured strings on \u0060VoiceConversationOptions\u0060, not CLR message types.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-VOICE-004","Title":"Interactive Presence Signals on Stream State Changes","Body":"On interactive stream disconnect, the runtime SHALL send \u0060User is AFK.\u0060 to the associated interactive agent session.\nOn interactive stream reconnect, after response stream establishment, the runtime SHALL send \u0060User is here.\u0060 to the associated interactive agent session.\n\nPresence signaling SHALL be excluded from one-shot sessions.\n\n**Status:** \uD83D\uDD34 Planned\n\n**Covered by:** \u0060VoiceConversationService\u0060 *(planned extension)*, \u0060AgentPoolStreamService\u0060 *(planned)*","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WEB-001","Title":"Web UI Ownership Boundary","Body":"Web UI implementation work for the former McpServer.UI.Core and McpServer.Director surfaces SHALL be owned by the McpServerManager repository. This repository SHALL keep only server-side contracts, API behavior, and compatibility documentation required by those external UI clients.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"deferred","Notes":"Deferred to McpServerManager; this repository owns only server-side contracts and compatibility documentation.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC1","text":"New Web UI implementation code is not added under this repository moved UI surfaces.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred to McpServerManager."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC2","text":"Server-side API changes needed by McpServerManager are tracked as MCP FR/TR/TEST items in this repository.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-001-AC3","text":"Cross-repo handoffs identify the owning repository and do not silently reopen moved UI projects here.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WEB-002","Title":"Web UI API Compatibility Contract","Body":"Server APIs consumed by external web-management clients SHALL remain documented and version-compatible across McpServer and McpServerManager. Breaking API changes require explicit requirements updates, migration notes, and tests in the server repository before deployment.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"deferred","Notes":"Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC1","text":"API changes intended for web-management clients name the consuming route, DTO, and owning client surface.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC2","text":"Breaking changes include a migration note and compatibility test coverage.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-002-AC3","text":"Generated requirements/wiki output reflects the current cross-repo API contract.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WEB-003","Title":"Web UI Authentication And Workspace Boundary","Body":"External web-management clients SHALL authenticate through the existing MCP workspace auth/token model and SHALL preserve workspace isolation. This repository SHALL provide the server-side policy and tests; client UX and screen implementation remain in McpServerManager.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"deferred","Notes":"Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC1","text":"Web-client API calls use existing workspace-token/OIDC policy behavior rather than a new parallel auth path.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC2","text":"Workspace-scoped requests remain isolated by the resolved workspace path.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-003-AC3","text":"Any new server endpoint used by web clients includes auth and workspace-isolation tests.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WEB-004","Title":"Web UI Deployment And Handoff Documentation","Body":"Deployment guidance for web-management surfaces SHALL distinguish server deployment in this repository from UI/client deployment in McpServerManager. This repository SHALL document only the server prerequisites, endpoint contracts, and compatibility expectations needed for the external UI.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"deferred","Notes":"Deferred until the next McpServerManager integration slice.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC1","text":"Server deployment docs do not instruct agents to deploy moved UI projects from this repository.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC2","text":"Handoff docs name McpServerManager as the owner for UI implementation and client deployment.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."},{"id":"TR-MCP-WEB-004-AC3","text":"Server readiness/config validation covers the endpoints and auth policy that external UI clients depend on.","isSatisfied":false,"evidence":"Deferred until next integration slice."}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001","Title":"docs/wiki.yaml export configuration loader and renderer integration","Body":"Implement a typed YamlDotNet-backed docs/wiki.yaml loader, validation layer, and wiki renderer integration shared by database-backed and document-backed requirements services.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"high","Status":"completed","Notes":"Do not parse YAML with string or regex logic. Resolve docs/wiki.yaml under the active workspace through RequirementsOptions.WikiConfigPath.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC1","text":"RequirementsOptions exposes WikiConfigPath defaulting to docs/wiki.yaml, and services resolve it under the active workspace path or configured requirements root.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC2","text":"RequirementsWikiExportConfig models deserialize docs/wiki.yaml with YamlDotNet into typed objects, with no line-based or regex YAML parsing.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC3","text":"Validation rejects unsupported schema values, missing required fields, duplicate document ids, duplicate targets per platform, path traversal, reserved managed target files, unsupported generated sources, invalid platform names, missing source files, and navigation/document mismatches.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC4","text":"Both RequirementsDatabaseDocumentService.GenerateWikiAsync and RequirementsDocumentService.GenerateWikiAsync share the same config loader and renderer path.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC5","text":"The exporter validates all configured content before calling RequirementsDocumentExportWriter so invalid config leaves existing export files unchanged.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-001-AC6","text":"Generated platform side files remain managed by the exporter, including .mcp-requirements-manifest.json, GitHub _Sidebar.md and _Footer.md, and Azure .order files.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002","Title":"Marker writer default wiki.yaml serializer","Body":"Extend MarkerFileService.WriteMarkerAsync with an idempotent default wiki.yaml writer that builds typed objects and serializes them with YamlDotNet before writing docs/wiki.yaml.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"high","Status":"completed","Notes":"The writer must run as part of marker creation and must preserve user-authored docs/wiki.yaml files.","AcceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC1","text":"MarkerFileService computes the default wiki config path as workspace-root/docs/wiki.yaml and creates the docs directory when needed.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC2","text":"MarkerFileService checks for an existing docs/wiki.yaml before writing and skips creation when the file already exists.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC3","text":"Default wiki config is represented by typed or dictionary objects and serialized with the existing YamlDotNet serializer.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC4","text":"The default config targets Home.md, Functional-Requirements.md, Technical-Requirements.md, Testing-Requirements.md, TR-per-FR-Mapping.md, and Requirements-Matrix.md on both platforms.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null},{"id":"TR-MCP-WIKIEXPORT-002-AC5","text":"A failure to create the default wiki.yaml is logged through the marker writer warning path and does not leave a partially written file.","isSatisfied":true,"evidence":null}],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-002","Title":"Workspace Service","Body":"CRUD operations for workspace entities persisted in EF Core SQLite. Auto-port assignment starts at base 7147 and increments from the current maximum registered port. Init scaffolding creates the workspace directory, \u0060docs/Project/TODO.yaml\u0060, \u0060docs/sessions/\u0060, \u0060docs/external/\u0060, and \u0060mcp.db\u0060.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-003","Title":"Workspace Process Manager","Body":"Manages workspace marker file lifecycle. On startup, generates tokens and writes \u0060AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml\u0060 marker files for all registered workspaces - all pointing to the single shared host port. On stop, removes marker files. No longer spawns child \u0060WebApplication\u0060 instances (replaced by single-app multi-tenant model, see TR-MCP-MT-001 through TR-MCP-MT-003).","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-004","Title":"Workspace Controller","Body":"REST API at \u0060/mcpserver/workspace\u0060 with Base64URL-encoded path keys. Provides create, read, update, delete, init, start, stop, status, and prompt (GET/PUT) endpoints. All \u0060/mcpserver/*\u0060 routes protected by \u0060WorkspaceAuthMiddleware\u0060 (per-workspace token).","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-005","Title":"Marker File Service","Body":"\u0060MarkerFileService.WriteMarkerAsync\u0060 writes \u0060AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml\u0060 to the workspace root. All markers point to the same shared host port. Uses Handlebars.Net templating with full workspace context. The marker template MUST be loaded from \u0060templates/prompt-templates.yaml\u0060 via \u0060PromptTemplateService\u0060 (id: \u0060default-marker-prompt\u0060). **CRITICAL**: If the template cannot be loaded (missing file, invalid YAML, or missing ID), the service must log a critical error and shut down the server immediately. Fallback to hardcoded templates is PROHIBITED. The YAML file contains port, \u0060baseUrl\u0060, all endpoint paths, process PID, \u0060startedAt\u0060 timestamp, workspace name, per-workspace auth token (\u0060apiKey\u0060), and a machine-readable \u0060prompt\u0060 block. Agents should send \u0060X-Workspace-Path\u0060 header for workspace targeting.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-006","Title":"Workspace Host Controller Isolation","Body":"*Obsolete.* Replaced by single-app multi-tenant model (TR-MCP-MT-002). \u0060ExcludeControllerFeatureProvider\u0060 can be removed.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-007","Title":"Workspace Auto-Start on Service Startup","Body":"\u0060WorkspaceProcessManager\u0060, as an \u0060IHostedService\u0060, queries all registered workspaces on \u0060StartAsync\u0060 and writes marker files for each. Failures on individual workspace marker writes are logged and skipped rather than aborting global startup.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-008","Title":"Workspace Auto-Init and Auto-Start on Creation","Body":"\u0060WorkspaceController\u0060 POST calls \u0060WorkspaceService.InitAsync\u0060 to scaffold the directory structure, then calls \u0060WorkspaceProcessManager.StartAsync\u0060 to bring the host online, all within a single request, before returning 201 Created.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id":"TR-MCP-WS-009","Title":"Primary Workspace Detection and IsEnabled Gating","Body":"\u0060WorkspaceProcessManager.IHostedService.StartAsync\u0060 resolves the primary workspace: first by \u0060IsPrimary = true\u0060 \u002B lowest port among enabled workspaces; then by lowest-port enabled workspace if none is marked primary. For the primary workspace, only a marker file is written - no child \u0060WebApplication\u0060 is created. Workspaces with \u0060IsEnabled = false\u0060 are skipped during auto-start but can be started manually.","WorkspaceId":"F:\\GitHub\\McpServer","Priority":"medium","Status":"pending","Notes":null,"AcceptanceCriteria":[],"ScopeStartLayerKey":"layer-1","ScopeEndLayerKey":null},{"Id